nsuranceappraiser.com/property-claim-services/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Hurricane & Nor’easter Appraisal","item":"https://marylandinsuranceappraiser.com/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/"}],"@id":"https://marylandinsuranceappraiser.com/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does appraisal decide whether my damage was wind or flood?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Appraisal values the amount of covered loss under your property policy. If the insurer says damage was caused by flood rather than wind, that causation and coverage dispute may need the carrier, the Maryland Insurance Administration or an attorney."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a nor’easter subject to my hurricane deductible in Maryland?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually not, because most hurricane deductibles are triggered by named tropical storms. Some policies use a broader windstorm deductible, so check the exact definition on your declarations page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the hurricane deductible itself be appraised?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The deductible percentage is a policy term, not a valuation item. What appraisal can do is make sure the loss amount the deductible is subtracted from reflects all covered damage."}}],"@id":"https://marylandinsuranceappraiser.com/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/#faq"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Hurricane & Nor’easter Appraisal","serviceType":"Maryland hurricane damage appraisal","description":"Hurricane, tropical storm or nor’easter claim disputed? Maryland appraisal for Bay and coastal wind losses, with your hurricane deductible checked.","provider":{"@id":"https://marylandinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"State","name":"Maryland"},"url":"https://marylandinsuranceappraiser.com/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appr